cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "FM-Bench: a football-club management game as a long-horizon LLM agent benchmark"
message: "If you use FM-Bench, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  # Institutional byline, matching the paper (\author{Analogy AI Research};
  # the individual author list is withheld until release). Replace with the
  # individual authors here and on the paper together, once that block is
  # finalized.
  - name: "Analogy AI Research"
    email: "support@analogyai.org"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Analogy-AI/fm-bench"
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.3"
abstract: >-
  FM-Bench is a deterministic, headless football-club management simulation
  used as a benchmark for long-horizon LLM agent decision-making. Agents run a
  fictional club for 5 to 20 in-game years across hundreds of decision stops
  under hidden information (true player ability is never revealed, only noisy
  and permanently-biased scout bands), delayed rewards, recoverable death
  spirals, a counter-adaptive transfer market, and multi-objective board
  pressure. Runs are scored by an uncapped log-compressed composite over
  honors, net-worth value added, and squad value. seed + action log = a
  bit-identical replay, which is the basis for audit and anti-cheat.
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - large-language-models
  - llm-agents
  - long-horizon
  - agent-evaluation
  - simulation
